NOTICE
======

This repository mixes material with two different owners, which is why it
carries a NOTICE rather than a conventional open-source licence. Applying MIT
or Apache here would purport to grant rights over documentation that is not
mine to grant.

What this is
------------
An unofficial, personal mirror of insightsoftware's published Logi Report and
JReport documentation, maintained by Amin Hasan so the corpus can be searched
offline and answered from with the version era attached to every page. It is
not an insightsoftware product, not an official distribution, and not endorsed
by insightsoftware.

insightsoftware material
------------------------
Logi Report, JReport, Logi Composer, Logi Info, Simba Intelligence and Dundas
are insightsoftware products. Everything under docs/ is insightsoftware's own
documentation, converted from HTML to Markdown with the source URL recorded in
each file's frontmatter. The Server Web API definition under api/spec/ is the
vendor's own file, copied byte-for-byte out of a running server. None of it is
relicensed by anything in this repository, and none of it is mine to relicense.

The licence position, stated plainly
------------------------------------
The three source help centres are publicly readable, and the crawler policy on
the current hosts permits fetching the article paths and the help centre API.
A crawler policy is not a redistribution licence. No terms-of-use page granting
one was found on any of the three hosts, so this mirror is published without an
express permission to redistribute and without claiming one. It exists because
the material is already public and a searchable local copy is useful. If
insightsoftware would rather it were not here, it comes down.

Original work
-------------
The orientation, API and task material written over the corpus is mine:
README.md, ORIENTATION.md, CONSUMING.md, CLAUDE.md, API-SURFACE.md, the authored
files under api/ and building-reports/, and the tooling in scripts/
(pull_docs.py, build_index.py, verify_kb.py, verify_api.py). Colleagues and
anyone else are welcome to clone, fork, pin and open issues against those.
Where an authored file states a fact, it names the source document it came from,
and the gates check that those citations still resolve.

Not here
--------
No credentials of any kind: no licence keys, tokens, passwords or host details.
No customer names, deployed customer artefacts or NDA-tagged material. No
product binaries, jars or installers. No internal issue-tracker keys, wiki page
identifiers or unreleased roadmap material; an earlier revision carried some and
it was removed before this repository was shared. Removing it from the working
tree does not remove it from git history, and that is a separate decision.

